csvlens is a terminal CSV file viewer with scrolling, searching,
filtering, sorting, and clipboard support.

Building requires rust-opt (Rust 1.88 or newer). Dependencies are
provided in a separate vendor archive; compilation runs offline using
the upstream Cargo.lock. Rust is not needed to run the built program.

Run "csvlens file.csv", or pipe CSV data into csvlens. Press "?" for
key bindings and "q" to quit. Use "csvlens --help" for command options.

Clipboard support is enabled. Copying with "y" requires an accessible
X11 or Wayland clipboard; viewing CSV files does not require a desktop.
